    "title": "pandas.Timestamp.asm8 — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1662.g0c49719283 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Timestamp.asm8#\n\n- Timestamp.asm8#\n- Return numpy datetime64 format with same precision. This property provides interoperability with NumPy datetime operations. See also \n  - `numpy.datetime64`\n  - Numpy datatype for dates and times with high precision.\n  - `Timestamp.to_numpy`\n  - Convert the Timestamp to a NumPy datetime64.\n  - `to_datetime`\n  - Convert argument to datetime.\n Examples >>> ts = pd.Timestamp(2020, 3, 14, 15) >>> ts.asm8 np.datetime64('2020-03-14T15:00:00.000000')",
